    "title_english": "正 — campaign, correction, and rightness",
    "summary_english": "Originally the graph for 征, a campaign against a walled settlement, 正 developed the senses ‘to pacify’, ‘to correct’, ‘right’, and ‘standard’.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "正",
      "pronunciation": "zhēng章纽、耕部；章纽、清韵、诸盈切。\nzhèng章纽、耕部；章纽、劲韵、之盛切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲文编》62页",
        "《金文编》88页",
        "《战文编》88页",
        "《说文》39页",
        "《睡甲》18页",
        "《马王堆》61页",
        "《甲金篆》98页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "会意字。甲骨文作﹑，从止，从囗，囗像城邑之形，会征伐城邑之意，乃“征”之初文，本义是征伐。\n《佚》18：“贞：勿唯王正方，上下弗若，不我其受佑？”\n邐方鼎\n（《集成》2709）\n：“唯王正井方。”均用征伐之本义。字亦借指岁之首月，即农历一年的第一个月，称为“正月”。引申为历法的代称，如说“夏正”即指夏历，“周正”指周历，因其建首之月不同。字还可借指箭靶的中心。以上诸义读为zhēng。征伐的目的就是有所平定﹑有所纠正，因而引申出平定﹑匡正义，由平定引申出决定﹑考定﹑勘定等义。由匡正引申出使端正义，进一步引申为治理义，进行治理的人亦称为“正”，进一步引申为准则﹑法则义。由官长之“正”，引申为正﹑副之“正”，进一步引申为嫡庶之称，嫡为正。《说文》训“正，是也”，乃引申义。“正”所从城邑之形“囗”或写实作黑点。黑点在西周金文中或简化为一横，春秋金文或在横上另加短横为饰，作，为《说文》古文“󶀌”所本，《说文》另一古文“󴮴”，从一﹑足，是由“󶀌”形讹变而来。“正”现在成了一个不象形的会意字。\n（陈英杰）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "An associative compound. Oracle-bone forms consist of 止 and 囗, the latter resembling a walled settlement; together they mean campaigning against a settlement. It is the original graph of 征, and its original sense is ‘to undertake a military expedition’. 《佚》18：“贞：勿唯王正方，上下弗若，不我其受佑？” 邐方鼎（《集成》2709）：“唯王正井方。” both use this primary sense.",
        "The character was also borrowed for the first month of the year, 正月, and hence for a calendar, as in 夏正 and 周正, which differ in the month with which they begin. It can also denote the center of an archery target. These uses are read zhēng. Since the purpose of a campaign is to bring things under control or set them right, it developed ‘to pacify’ and ‘to correct’; from the former, ‘to determine’, ‘to verify’, and ‘to survey’, and from the latter, ‘to make upright’, then ‘to govern’. A person who governs may also be called 正, and this further produced ‘rule’ and ‘standard’.",
        "From 正 as an official superior came the contrast of principal and deputy, and then the designation of the legitimate line as 正 in contrast to collateral lines. 《说文》’s gloss ‘正，是也’ is an extended meaning. The enclosure component can be written realistically as a black dot, simplified to a horizontal line in Western Zhou bronzes, or given an ornamental short stroke in Spring-and-Autumn forms; these are the basis of the ancient forms recorded in 《说文》. The modern graph is thus an associative compound no longer transparently pictographic. （陈英杰）"
      ]
    },
