    "summary_english": "An associative character derived from a half-form of 冓 with an added stroke, used from early writing for twice, second, repetition, addition, and subsequent action.",
    "etymology": {
      "available": true,
      "headword": "再",
      "pronunciation": "zài精纽、之部；精纽、代韵、作代切。",
      "bibliography": [
        "《甲文编》191页",
        "《金文编》267页",
        "《郭店》72页",
        "《说文》83页",
        "《睡甲》57页",
        "《马王堆》152页"
      ],
      "explanation_original": "会意字。初文从形\n（冓字对半之省形）\n，上部加一横笔。周代文字又或累加横笔或口形为饰。早期字形中的形后世渐写作平直，而为秦篆所本。古文献及古文字材料中，“再”字可用表两次﹑第二次。\n《说文》：“再，一举而二也。”\n𠫑羌钟：“唯廿又再祀。”\n（二十又二年）\n陈喜壶：“𬯔\n（陈）\n喜再立事岁。”\n（陈喜第二次莅临政事这年）\n引申有重复﹑继续义。\n唐杜甫《自京赴奉先县咏怀五百字》：“荣枯咫尺异，惆怅难再述。”\n又可引申为另﹑另外义，用表另有补充。\n唐李白《溧阳濑水贞义女碑铭》：“皇唐叶有六圣，再造八极。”\n表示动作的先后关系，“再”还可引申为然后义。\n《红楼梦》第四十一回：“\n（把杯子）\n取来再商量。”\n（齐航福）",
      "images_omitted": true,
      "explanation_english": [
        "再 is an associative character. Its earliest form is a reduced half of 冓 with an added horizontal stroke. Zhou forms may add further strokes or mouth-shaped ornamentation. The early curved component was gradually written straight, producing the Qin small-seal ancestor. In transmitted texts and excavated writing, 再 denotes two times or a second occurrence. 《说文》 says “再，一举而二也。” 𠫑羌钟 records “唯廿又再祀。” meaning ‘twenty-two years’, and 陈喜壶 reads “𬯔（陈）喜再立事岁。” meaning the year Chen Xi took office for the second time.",
        "The word extended to repetition and continuation. Du Fu’s 《自京赴奉先县咏怀五百字》 says “荣枯咫尺异，惆怅难再述。” It can also mean ‘another; additionally’, as in Li Bai’s 《溧阳濑水贞义女碑铭》, “皇唐叶有六圣，再造八极。” Marking the sequence of actions, it further developed the sense ‘then; afterwards’: 《红楼梦》第四十一回 has “（把杯子）取来再商量。” (Qi Hangfu)"
      ]
    },
